annote={Strains of Y. pombe in isolation had the same absolute growthrates, but pairwise competition revealed differences among strains. Pairwise fitness assays (but not monoculture growthrates) were pretty good at predicting community outcomes over evolutionary timescales (300+ generations). Also saw that strains in multispecies communities were more likely to develop maladptations to their env (tradeoffs between biotic and abiotic tolerance?). Emphasizes pairwise competition as predictive of community level outcomes.}
}
